From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gngpp <gngppz@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] boringssl: skip compiler-generated helpers in the symbol audit

Auditing libssl, not just libcrypto, reaches the helper functions the compiler
emits for C++ code, such as MSVC's array constructor and destructor iterators.
They belong to the compiler runtime rather than BoringSSL, carry no identifier
prefixing could rewrite, and being weak they merge instead of colliding. The
surrounding list already skips their siblings, `__cxa_*`, the unwinder
personalities and the RTTI records.

